add('The required demonstration registers all three roles, approves both providers, uploads the supplied fictional note, shows a denied doctor request before sharing, grants doctor access, verifies decrypted bytes, shares independently with the hospital, revokes the doctor and records a second denial. The hospital permission remains independent. The supplied execution transcript captures these actions against a real local contract and IPFS stores.')
add('Browser layout was inspected, and the shared cryptographic/client workflows were executed in integration tests. Full browser encryption interactions were not verified in the remote insecure HTTP preview. The localhost deployment is the supported student demonstration environment; the report does not claim that the browser workflow passed an end-to-end automation test.')

page('7. Audit semantics and security evaluation')
add('Registration, provider-status changes, ownership creation, grants and revocations produce immutable contract events. The gateway auditor also emits ReadAudit for both allowed and denied authenticated requests. Denied reads do not revert, because a reverted transaction would discard its event. An allowed event means the gateway approved a request at that point; it does not prove successful delivery or human viewing. Later storage failures are represented by the gateway response and its outcome log.')
add('The gateway writes a hash-linked local JSONL log containing time, route, authenticated actor, response status and the previous entry hash. This is useful for checking continuity but is not an independently anchored ledger. An operator who can replace the complete file can rewrite its history. Direct IPFS ciphertext fetches, offline decryption and reverted direct contract transactions are outside the complete gateway audit scope. The dashboard shows the latest 150 events; full event history remains accessible through RPC.')
table(['Threat / property','Control and observed result'],[['Unauthorized role escalation','Non-administrator provider approval rejected; duplicate registration rejected'],['Unauthorized file sharing','Owner-only contract checks reject provider grants; unapproved providers rejected'],['Missing, revoked or expired consent','Gateway refuses reads; corresponding read decisions are preserved on-chain'],['Provider suspension','Active grants become unusable until eligibility is restored'],['Ciphertext / envelope tampering','AES-GCM, SHA-256 commitments and envelope checks reject altered values'],['Wrong recipient private key','RSA unwrap fails; another registered provider cannot use that envelope'],['Signed-request replay or substitution','Consumed nonce and signed body/route/contract scope reject a second or changed request'],['Forged audit event','Non-auditor callers cannot invoke logRead'],['Previously downloaded copy','Still decryptable after revocation; explicitly tested and disclosed']],[157,W-157])
sub('Test evidence')
add('The submitted suite contains 22 functional and security checks. Expected rejection is a passing result when the test asserts that an unauthorized action must fail. Tests use a freshly deployed contract and compare decrypted bytes with their original synthetic input. The evidence folder retains the TAP log and deployment information. These checks establish the specified behaviors; they are not a substitute for static analysis, fuzzing, independent penetration testing or formal verification.')

