sub('Interpretation')
add('Effective prices vary by signer and local base fee. The benchmark auditor uses an unlocked RPC signer whose local default price becomes extremely small; its near-zero fee is not a realistic public-chain read price. At a common 2 gwei, the mean read-audit gas would cost '+f"{OPS['read_audit']['gas']['mean']*2e9/1e18:.8f}"+' ETH. Compare gas for implementation efficiency and use an explicit common price for fee forecasts.')
add('Deployment is paid once per contract instance. Public encryption-key strings make registration relatively storage-intensive. A record stores only a CID and fixed-size commitments, so medical-file size mainly affects encryption and storage transfer rather than on-chain bytes. A first permission grant writes a new mapping entry; revocation deletes it and the receipt accounts for the applicable gas-refund rules. Access auditing itself consumes gas, even when clinical data is read rather than modified.')
add('A complete upload or share workflow contains more than one activity. The ownership-creation row is only the blockchain part of upload. Sharing also incurs an owner read-audit transaction, while provider retrieval incurs its own read-audit transaction. IPFS storage, gateway hosting and key management have operational costs outside these ETH figures. Raw transaction hashes, gas used, effective prices, fees and measured latencies are available in transactions.csv.')

